From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:55:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the AOP ambient light and lid
 angle services

The AOP core (soc: apple: aop) registers a platform device for each sensor
service the firmware announces and gives it the AOP child node of the same
name, if that node is available. The T8132 AOP node has an audio child only,
so the als and las services of the J604 firmware stay unbound.

Add the two children, disabled, as T604x describes them (t604x.dtsi), so a
board enables the services its firmware has. No board enables them here.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 1bd4acdf78..15cb0a8ebd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -1334,6 +1334,22 @@
 				dma-names = "dma";
 				#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
 			};
+
+			/*
+			 * Sensor services of the AOP firmware. The AOP core gives
+			 * each service it registers the child named like it, and
+			 * only an available one, so a board enables the services
+			 * its firmware announces.
+			 */
+			aop_als: als {
+				compatible = "apple,t8132-aop-als", "apple,aop-als";
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
+
+			aop_las: las {
+				compatible = "apple,t8132-aop-las", "apple,aop-las";
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
 		};
 
 		/* ADT lists the interrupts as 1, 0, 3, 2 of the block: send-empty is the lowest. */
